# Step 07 — Release artifact CI

## Purpose
Add GitHub Actions automation that builds the macOS app in Release configuration and uploads the unsigned `Spotiglass.app` bundle directly as a workflow artifact (no manual zip step). This step follows app polish because CI should package the real app surface, not an incomplete scaffold.

## Stack / tech locked in this step
- GitHub Actions.
- macOS GitHub-hosted runner.
- Latest stable Xcode selection compatible with the macOS 26 SDK.
- `xcodebuild` for clean, test, and Release build operations as appropriate for an unsigned `.app`.
- Unsigned Release `Spotiglass.app` bundle uploaded directly with `actions/upload-artifact` (no `zip` packaging step in the workflow).
- No deployment, no notarization, no Developer ID signing, no App Store upload, and no GitHub Release publishing unless explicitly approved later.

## Tasks

- [x] **07.1** — Define local release build command
  - Identify the exact scheme, configuration, SDK, destination, and derived data path used to build the app.
  - Ensure the command produces a Release `.app` bundle without requiring signing credentials.
  - Keep Debug and Release build settings intentional and documented.
  - Expected output: a local command can create the same `.app` shape CI will upload.

- [x] **07.2** — Add CI workflow
  - Create `.github/workflows/release-artifact.yml`.
  - Trigger on manual `workflow_dispatch` only at this step's implementation; push and pull-request triggers were intentionally not added because no other CI workflow exists yet and the project owner asked to keep triggers conservative.
  - Select the latest stable Xcode available on the runner via `maxim-lobanov/setup-xcode`.
  - Run unit tests before packaging so the artifact only ships when tests pass.
  - Expected output: GitHub Actions can build and verify the app automatically.

- [x] **07.3** — Stage the unsigned `.app` for upload
  - Build the app in Release configuration with `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO`.
  - Locate the resulting `Spotiglass.app` deterministically under the derived-data path.
  - Stage the `.app` bundle at the workspace root so its directory layout is preserved when uploaded.
  - Do **not** create a manual `.zip` of the bundle; the workflow uploads the `.app` directory directly.
  - Expected output: the workflow leaves a single `Spotiglass.app` bundle ready for the upload step, with its universal `arm64 + x86_64` Mach-O binary intact.

- [x] **07.4** — Upload workflow artifact
  - Use `actions/upload-artifact@v4` with the `path` set to the staged `Spotiglass.app` directory.
  - Set artifact name `Spotiglass-release-app` and a 14-day retention policy.
  - Use `if-no-files-found: error` so a missing `.app` fails the workflow loudly.
  - Do not upload secrets, derived-data caches containing credentials, or build logs containing tokens.
  - Expected output: each successful workflow run exposes `Spotiglass.app` as a downloadable artifact bundle. GitHub serves workflow artifacts as a zip download by default; the workflow itself does not perform any zip packaging.

- [x] **07.5** — Document unsigned app expectations
  - Document that the artifact is unsigned beyond the ad-hoc linker signature and may require local macOS security approval to open.
  - Document that no notarization or Developer ID signing is performed in this step.
  - Document the trigger model (`workflow_dispatch`-only), the artifact name, and how to download and launch the `.app`.
  - Expected output: users understand the artifact's distribution limitations.

- [x] **07.6** — Verify CI locally and remotely
  - Run the local Release build command end-to-end and confirm the `Spotiglass.app` bundle is produced unsigned.
  - Run the unit-test suite locally.
  - Validate the GitHub Actions workflow syntax with `actionlint` (which integrates `shellcheck` for inline shell steps).
  - Remote workflow execution is deferred until the user explicitly authorizes a push that runs the workflow on GitHub-hosted runners.
  - Expected output: CI is ready without performing unauthorized deploys or pushes.

- [x] **07.7** — Update roadmap state
  - Mark every task checkbox in this step file as `[x]` after completion.
  - Mark Step 7 as `[x]` in `.cursor/rules/ROADMAP.mdc`.
  - Expected output: roadmap state accurately reflects Step 7 completion.

## Done criteria
- [x] A GitHub Actions workflow builds the app with a latest stable Xcode setup.
- [x] Unit tests run before packaging, so a failing test blocks the artifact upload.
- [x] The workflow produces an unsigned Release `Spotiglass.app` bundle with no manual zip step.
- [x] The `.app` bundle is uploaded as a workflow artifact via `actions/upload-artifact@v4`.
- [x] The workflow does not deploy, notarize, sign with private credentials, publish a GitHub Release, or push changes.
- [x] Local build verification is complete and documented in `README.md`.
